PKG=modtools
NAME=modtools 1.0.261104-14 - load, unload and inspect kernel modules
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.0.261104-14
CATEGORY=system
CLASSES=none
VENDOR=amix-packages
PSTAMP=amix-packages-modtools-1.0.261104-14
# USERLAND (C2-4 v8 sec 11): an ordinary catalog entry, no
# kpkg entry, no apkg kernel-space record, no catalog dependency -- modadmin
# reaches the module core through system calls; on a static kernel it fails
# at run time, which is correct.
APKG_DESC=modadmin: load, unload, list and inspect kernel modules; read or write a loaded module's tunables by name; print or keep the kernel's message buffer (/sbin/modadmin, static)
APKG_ESSENTIAL=yes
DESC=The module administrator of the amix-dlm module core: loads and unloads kernel modules, lists them and shows their status, registers driver majors for load on first open, loads the boot-class modules from the first sysinit entry of /etc/inittab (modadmin -B; the line is amix-base's inittab, the package has no scripts), and reads or writes a loaded module's tunables and counters by symbol name through /dev/kmem, prints the kernel's message buffer (modadmin -L) and keeps kernel messages in it on a box with no console logger (modadmin -K, root).  Since -10 the status of a module that cannot be unloaded (unload=never, shown locked) says its unload delay is never, not the default 60 seconds the core never uses.  Needs a module kernel.  Statically linked, GCC 14; built from amix 9be1705; MIT.
